WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.350
CLASS 2

00:00.470 --> 00:04.350
There are just too many dangerous 
factors in this world.

00:04.640 --> 00:06.810
What was that explosion the other day?

00:06.810 --> 00:12.170
We can't have someone going around 
using dangerous magic like that.

00:12.170 --> 00:15.950
Megumin does it every day, though.

00:15.950 --> 00:19.310
Megumin doesn't count. 
She never causes any harm...

00:20.390 --> 00:21.830
She never...

00:22.420 --> 00:24.990
Tanya, you don't have to force yourself to lie.

00:24.990 --> 00:30.670
Anyway, what I'm trying to say is that it's 
possible to read "we should all be friends"

00:30.670 --> 00:34.250
as "we can harm anyone but our classmates."

00:34.250 --> 00:36.970
I've come to the same conclusion.

00:36.970 --> 00:40.050
We'll have to change how we 
think about external enemies.

00:41.290 --> 00:43.980
I'm not sure it's that deep.

00:44.560 --> 00:52.090
The guy who used that magic might've just 
wanted to say, "I can use cool spells, too!"

00:52.090 --> 00:54.590
Maybe we don't have anything 
to worry about at all.

00:56.070 --> 01:00.290
Kazuma, you should take this 
a little more seriously.

01:00.290 --> 01:03.010
That's right. You're far too calm about this.

01:03.010 --> 01:04.960
Wow, you guys are harsh!

01:10.170 --> 01:17.790
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:31.590 --> 02:35.040
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:35.050 --> 02:40.070
#03: Working Together! Morning Glories

02:35.810 --> 02:37.630
Growing morning glories?

02:37.630 --> 02:41.640
Yes. You will all work 
together to raise flowers.

02:41.640 --> 02:44.820
Doesn't that sound wonderful?

02:44.820 --> 02:45.520
Right?

02:45.520 --> 02:50.080
Yes. Growing flowers...
I think that's a great idea.

02:50.080 --> 02:53.030
Don't you think so, Albedo?

02:53.030 --> 02:58.300
Indeed. In the language of flowers, morning 
glories mean "love"! "Coming together"!

02:58.300 --> 03:04.250
Hand-in-hand with Ains-sama, 
working together to raise our love!

03:05.630 --> 03:08.290
And so...

03:08.290 --> 03:13.890
Wait! Wait, Roswaal! Roswaal-sensei!

03:09.410 --> 03:13.430
Like always, we'll be deciding it by...

03:13.890 --> 03:15.130
A drawing!

03:15.130 --> 03:15.850
I wonder.

03:15.850 --> 03:16.970
Correct.

03:25.140 --> 03:28.090
Mare, I should've known you'd be great at this!

03:28.090 --> 03:31.770
Hmph! I could do that if I wanted to!

03:32.040 --> 03:33.340
Nah, no way.

03:33.340 --> 03:35.350
To raise a flower, you need love.

03:35.350 --> 03:39.060
But you give all your love to me, right?

03:39.060 --> 03:41.350
Wh-What are you talking about, I wonder?

03:41.350 --> 03:46.160
But... fine. I-I'll hold hands with you for now.

03:46.160 --> 03:49.490
That's my pretty Bea-ko!

03:49.490 --> 03:52.690
By the way, we don't need to hold hands.

03:50.090 --> 03:52.690
Of course I'm pretty!

03:52.690 --> 03:53.780
I see.

04:00.750 --> 04:04.470
Garfiel-dono, you can do the 
same things as Mare, huh?

04:04.470 --> 04:05.660
Yeah.

04:05.660 --> 04:08.670
I've got the Divine Protection 
of Earth Spirits.

04:08.670 --> 04:10.150
Nice.

04:11.070 --> 04:13.570
Aura, is something wrong?

04:13.570 --> 04:17.190
He's powerful, and a beastman.

04:18.930 --> 04:21.230
No, Aura.

04:21.230 --> 04:23.100
Oh, you could tell what I was thinking?

04:24.730 --> 04:25.890
What do you mean?

04:25.890 --> 04:28.830
Aura wanted you, Garfiel.

04:28.830 --> 04:31.080
"Wanted"?

04:31.080 --> 04:34.500
She just wants to add you to her collection.

04:34.930 --> 04:37.540
That's awful.

04:38.870 --> 04:42.620
Sorry, but I refuse to belong to anybody.

04:42.620 --> 04:44.260
Anybody at all?

04:44.260 --> 04:45.590
Yup!

04:45.590 --> 04:47.180
Really?

04:47.180 --> 04:50.840
I want to give myself heart 
and body to Ains-sama, though.

04:50.840 --> 04:51.770
Heart and body?!

04:52.150 --> 04:57.510
Isn't it kind of creepy to give your 
heart and body to someone, though?

04:57.510 --> 04:59.150
Not at all.

04:59.150 --> 05:00.430
Really?

05:00.430 --> 05:01.620
Yeah, really.

05:01.620 --> 05:03.750
Really, really?

05:03.470 --> 05:06.760
Ains is really popular, huh?

05:03.750 --> 05:05.630
Really, really!

05:06.760 --> 05:09.810
Yup. I'm jealous.

05:11.770 --> 05:16.290
I'm sure they're all using magic 
to make it grow instantly.

05:17.510 --> 05:19.840
But us, we're...

05:21.550 --> 05:23.300
Ordinary.

05:25.410 --> 05:28.580
Um, Kazuma, I was thinking...

05:28.580 --> 05:33.180
I don't think we need to 
use magic at all for this.

05:33.180 --> 05:34.990
Visha, what do you think?

05:34.990 --> 05:36.100
I know what you mean.

05:36.100 --> 05:41.460
We've been relying on magic and divine 
protections ever since we got here.

05:41.460 --> 05:45.590
Instead of growing them to be big, let's just 
grow our morning glories to be strong and pretty.

05:45.590 --> 05:46.840
Yes.

05:46.840 --> 05:50.170
It's sad that I can't do this with Ains-sama,

05:50.170 --> 05:54.330
but I think if I grow a beautiful flower 
and give it to him as a present,

05:54.330 --> 05:56.130
he'll really feel my love.

05:56.130 --> 05:57.750
So Kazuma,

05:58.020 --> 06:00.410
you'd better not slack off.

06:00.410 --> 06:01.750
Sure, sure.

06:01.750 --> 06:04.420
So in the end, you are using magic?

06:04.420 --> 06:05.450
Geez.

06:05.450 --> 06:09.880
Okay, I'll use my Divine Protection of the 
Soul of Language to keep the bugs away.

06:09.880 --> 06:12.270
So in the end, you're 
using divine protections?!

06:13.870 --> 06:15.930
Listen up, guys.

06:15.930 --> 06:20.550
With me, the goddess of water, at your side, 
we can't be allowed to lose!

06:20.550 --> 06:24.260
I don't like being paired 
up with undead and vampires,

06:24.260 --> 06:26.900
but let's work together to grow new life!

06:26.900 --> 06:32.970
If you want to grow life, 
you're talking to the wrong people.

06:32.970 --> 06:35.630
What a flower needs to grow is light and water!

06:35.630 --> 06:38.750
I can handle the water,

06:38.750 --> 06:42.040
so you, shine some light for us!

06:42.040 --> 06:47.360
We're not the ones to talk to if you need light.

06:47.360 --> 06:49.280
You can do it if you try hard enough!

06:49.280 --> 06:54.020
Just do it like this! Look! Look! Like this!

06:50.090 --> 06:52.700
This conversation's a huge waste of time.

06:52.700 --> 06:54.030
Just ignore them.

06:54.570 --> 06:57.770
What's with that look? You guys are so cold.

06:56.690 --> 06:59.740
With events like this, you can 
just leave it to the people

06:59.740 --> 07:01.810
who want to do it and it'll usually work out.

07:01.810 --> 07:05.650
Totally wrong! Totally wrong! 
That's totally wrong!

07:02.850 --> 07:06.660
Really? I don't know if that's always the case.

07:07.280 --> 07:10.530
When that happens, just make the people 
who did it take responsibility.

07:10.910 --> 07:14.010
I didn't do any of the work,
 so it's not my fault.

07:14.010 --> 07:18.830
I could learn a thing or two from you 
about getting along in the world.

07:16.660 --> 07:20.790
Totally wrong! Totally wrong! 
That's totally wrong!

07:20.790 --> 07:26.380
I've never grown any kind of plant,
 let alone a morning glory.

07:26.380 --> 07:27.920
Really?

07:27.920 --> 07:32.140
In my world, plants were precious.

07:32.870 --> 07:35.170
That's more of a dystopia than I imagined.

07:35.170 --> 07:37.890
You! Stop talking and work!

07:37.890 --> 07:39.010
Sheesh!

07:39.010 --> 07:44.380
Aqua-san, water and light aren't 
enough to raise a plant.

07:44.380 --> 07:46.910
They're not, narrow-faced man?

07:46.910 --> 07:49.140
Do you have any interest in learning my name?

07:50.030 --> 07:58.080
Um, for a morning glory, you need to 
make the plant think that it's night.

07:59.300 --> 08:04.150
That's you, Ains! You're the ruler 
of the darkness, so make it night!

08:04.150 --> 08:06.580
Who started calling me that?

08:06.580 --> 08:07.620
Just do it.

08:09.350 --> 08:12.430
I don't have any spells that 
can turn day into night...

08:15.390 --> 08:18.120
It's getting dark.

08:18.120 --> 08:19.680
It's night now!

08:19.680 --> 08:22.670
Ains! So you can do it if you try!

08:22.670 --> 08:25.290
No, this wasn't me.

08:25.810 --> 08:27.810
So who did it, then?

08:27.810 --> 08:30.950
It's not just time for the sun to set?

08:30.950 --> 08:32.290
Maybe you're right.

08:32.290 --> 08:36.150
Ains, all your effort was wasted.

08:36.150 --> 08:37.160
I keep telling you...

08:37.160 --> 08:38.540
Who's there?

08:42.780 --> 08:44.020
When did he show up?

08:49.110 --> 08:53.820
A world of light... 
A world shrouded in darkness...

08:53.820 --> 08:54.850
What?

08:55.300 --> 09:00.140
At the end of chaos... you will find shadow.

09:01.470 --> 09:03.940
You were the one earlier who...

09:02.450 --> 09:03.940
Hey, you.

09:04.390 --> 09:08.370
I don't understand a word you just said, 
but if something's bothering you, tell me.

09:08.370 --> 09:12.690
I, Aqua-sama, the goddess 
of water, shall guide you!

09:12.690 --> 09:15.110
Don't interrupt me, you self-proclaimed goddess!

09:16.130 --> 09:19.900
She called me "self-proclaimed," 
but I'm a real goddess!

09:19.900 --> 09:21.250
Are you still calling yourself that?!

09:21.250 --> 09:23.830
Calm down, both of you.

09:23.830 --> 09:24.410
Face...

09:24.410 --> 09:28.420
It's Koenig! When are you 
going to learn my name?

09:26.370 --> 09:28.420
Named, huh?

09:29.210 --> 09:31.470
Nice to meet you, I suppose.

09:31.900 --> 09:34.350
I am Ains Ooal Gown.

09:34.920 --> 09:38.030
Would you be so kind as to tell me your name?

09:38.410 --> 09:39.430
Shadow.

09:40.180 --> 09:41.410
Shadow?

09:41.810 --> 09:42.570
So...

09:42.570 --> 09:44.490
Ains Ooal Gown...

09:46.020 --> 09:47.150
Yes.

09:47.150 --> 09:48.890
Ruler of the darkness.

09:51.310 --> 09:52.410
Interesting.

09:54.060 --> 09:56.530
Does darkness lie beyond the shadow?

09:56.910 --> 09:59.580
Or is it shadows that end the darkness?

09:59.580 --> 10:02.600
Wait, I really don't get what you're saying.

10:02.600 --> 10:07.460
Or perhaps it is the light that rules all.

10:11.780 --> 10:14.140
He disappeared.

10:17.050 --> 10:18.830
So that happened.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.790
A man calling himself Shadow, huh?

10:22.790 --> 10:23.790
Yes.

10:23.790 --> 10:26.820
He said, "Does darkness lie beyond the shadow?"

10:26.820 --> 10:29.900
"Or is it shadows that end the darkness?", right?

10:29.900 --> 10:31.410
What's that supposed to mean?

10:31.410 --> 10:34.250
No idea. It might be some kind of code.

10:34.930 --> 10:38.570
For the moment, we don't have 
enough information to be sure.

10:38.970 --> 10:41.940
We'll need to look into this.

10:41.940 --> 10:47.690
Nah, I bet he just made that up to sound cool.

10:47.690 --> 10:50.540
"I'm such a badass. 
I've got such cool dialogue."

10:50.540 --> 10:51.500
Like that?

10:52.050 --> 10:55.610
Kazuma, you should take this 
a little more seriously.

10:55.610 --> 10:58.490
That's right. You're far too calm about this.

10:58.490 --> 11:00.190
Wow, you guys are harsh!

11:00.810 --> 11:04.850
Um, I got the same impression.

11:04.850 --> 11:07.260
Don't worry. So did I.
